\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Stronger Late; Following Bullish Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1999\par 11:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar has climbed against the U.S. dollar in late Asian trading Tuesday, riding on the coattails of the bullish Indonesian rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0940 GMT (5:40 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7090, weaker than S$1.7117 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah rose to its highest level since October, as foreign investors return to the country, encouraged by falling inflation and a peaceful campaign ahead of last week's parliamentary election. \par \par \uc2  "There's a total reassessment of the whole regional risk," a dealer at a European bank said, noting that Indonesia was now benefiting from the resurgence of investor inflows that its neighbors have seen in recent months. \par \par \uc2  Because of it's greater liquidity, the Singapore dollar often acts as a proxy for the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also said the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday had also supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's Monday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its third in as many days, was aimed at capping the yen's rise against the U.S. dollar in order to maintain Japan's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  The dealer at the European brokerage said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, the de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would closely watch the rupiah's advance in order to determine an appropriate level for the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  In recent months, the MAS has been following a policy of gradual depreciation for the Singapore dollar, but restored confidence in the rupiah could lead the MAS to yield on its stance, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said he expected the U.S. dollar to weaken below the key support level of S$1.7000 later this week if the rupiah continued its rally. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 0.875%, up from 0.125% late Monday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 1.625%, unchanged from late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0958GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6f04i6s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
