\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Higher Early; No Sign Of MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 1999\par 04:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is drifting higher against the U.S. dollar in thin trading early Tuesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore and local banks are, for the moment, taking a laissez-faire approach to the Singapore dollar's strength, letting the market determine the direction of the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "There are no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment," a trader at a U.K. bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  At 0145 GMT (9:45 p.m. Monday EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6984, down from S$1.6999 in late trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has been falling gradually against the Singapore dollar during the past three or four sessions, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The bulk of U.S. dollar selling appears to be done, and we should see some consolidation within a range today," said a trader at a U.S. investment house in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He expects the U.S. dollar to move between S$1.6950 and S$1.7035 during the session. "The MAS looks comfortable with the strength of the Singapore dollar, given that the region looks stable at the moment. It appears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will let the (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) drift higher as long as the pace isn't too quick." \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is expected to continue sliding this week unless regional news stirs up the markets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "We should see S$1.6850 by the end of the week," a trader at a Japanese bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  In the local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight offered rate on the Singapore dollar was 0.875%, up a touch from 0.75% Monday. The three-month rate was 1.50%, slightly up from 1.4375% late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Brian Truscott; 65 421 4800; btruscott@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-05-99 \par \par \uc2  0200GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5b03jir\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
