\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open Higher; More Baht Gains Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 1999\par 03:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have mostly opened a touch stronger against the U.S. dollar in early Asian trading Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  After the Thai baht (THB) hit a three-month high against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, lifted by continued inflows to the local stock market, traders are confidently predicting further gains in Asian hours Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Even with the Dow (Jones Industrial Average) down overnight, people are still pushing money into Thailand and Indonesia, so I expect the market to sell dollars against the baht and the rupiah," said a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a major U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  At 0050 GMT (8:50 p.m. EDT) the U.S. dollar is at THB36.8050, down from THB36.8700 late the day before in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah (IDR), the U.S. dollar is at IDR8,087 compared with IDR8,085 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  Although good U.S. dollar selling interest is reported at levels approaching IDR8,100, traders are wary of buying interest emerging below IDR8,000 from Indonesian players and offshore profit-takers. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.7017, down from S$1.7058 late in Asia the previous day. With fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  deterring potential U.S. dollar sellers, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to be supported at S$1.7000. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the Philippine peso has yet to begin. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4808; tom.holland@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-05-99 \par \par \uc2  0103GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5503g9b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
