\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Dn Late In Choppy Mkt, Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1999\par 10:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is weaker in late trading in Asia Thursday compared with a day earlier as suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down from intraday highs. \par \par \uc2  About 0845 GMT (4:45 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7016, up from S$1.6996 late Thursday in Asia and from a low early in the day of S$1.6929. \par \par \uc2  Trading was choppy Friday, with foreign names selling U.S. dollars against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on spikes, and local names buying on dips, one trader in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  A resurgent stock market and continued optimistic remarks by officials over the economy have lent the Singapore dollar strength, he said. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, the island-state's effective \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is suspected of stepping in to keep that strength in check. \par \par \uc2  Analysts believe the government is concerned that a strong Singapore dollar could further the country's trade competitiveness, which lost some ground early in the regional crisis. \par \par \uc2  Next week, traders expects the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stay within a fairly broad band of S$1.6900 to S$1.7200 in continued choppy trading. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.250%, up from 0.6725% late Thursday, while the three-month rate was offered at 1.250%, up from 1.1875%. \par \par \uc2  -By Roger Malone; 65-421 4800; rmalone@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0854GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4u03au0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
