\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: Singapore Dlr Sentiment Improves \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 1999\par 10:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar also benefited from positive investor sentiment, despite a moderate sell off in the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like sentiment has changed. What we are seeing is a sound rally in the Singapore dollar," said a trader at a local bank, adding: "With no big sellers around, I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to get stronger." \par \par \uc2  In recent sessions market participants have held back from buying the Singapore dollar for fear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down, should it strengthen too far on a trade-weighted basis. \par \par \uc2  But as the Singapore dollar's continuing bull-run has failed to prompt MAS action, traders have become more confident about the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's prospects. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone was expecting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But I don't think the MAS is likely to come in if the rest of the Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also getting stronger," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  Towards the end of Asian trading the U.S. dollar had been sold down to S$1.6953, from S$1.6988 a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  Strong support for the U.S. dollar should emerge at levels between S$1.6900 and S$1.6920, said traders. But if S$1.6900 is broken, "We are on the way back to the S$1.56 level," according to one bullish dealer. Others expect firm support at S$1.6550. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah (IDR) the U.S. dollar dropped to IDR8,548, down from IDR8,603, as some dealers reported rupiah purchases from offshore players in search of handsome double digit yields. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 28-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0838GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4s0374h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
