\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Stronger Early As Stk Mkt Gains Lend Support \b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 1999\par 03:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is stronger in early trade Wednesday in Asia against the U.S. dollar supported by an equities rally and reduced fears of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  About 0130 GMT (9:30 p.m. Tuesday EST), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.6962, down from S$1.6984 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  "The buoyancy in the stock market is causing some selling interest in dollar-Sing," one trader at a Asian bank in Singapore said. "This is all riding on the buoyancy of the stock market." \par \par \uc2  Since early February, the benchmark index on the Stock Exchange of Singapore has risen almost 50%, triggering an inflow of funds. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, steady or strengthening regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have reduced the chances of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar strength, the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Although immediate support for the U.S. dollar is around S$1.6950, reportedly buttressed by local bank buying, some see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling as low as S$1.66 in the near term before resuming its upward trend. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight offered rate was at 0.375%, up from 0.3125% late Tuesday, while the three-month offered rate was at 1.250%, unchanged from late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Roger Malone; 65/421 4800; rmalone@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-04-99 \par 