\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Mkts Rocked By New Yuan Fear \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended a whipsaw trading session on Tuesday mixed against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  After trailing the yen higher throughout the Asian morning, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw an abrupt sell-off in afternoon dealing on resurgent fears of a Chinese yuan devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Market participants scampered to buy U.S. dollars after rumors emerged that the Shanghai branch of the People's Bank of China had initiated a study to investigate the economic impact of a possible devaluation of the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Shanghai sources stressed that Beijing's commitment to a stable yuan remains rock-solid and emphasized that the PBOC study was being conducted solely as an independent academic exercise. Nevertheless, rumors of the study were sufficient to trigger a bout of dollar-buying against both the yen and the freely-traded Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In North Asia, both the South Korean won and the New Taiwan dollar recovered from their intraday lows to end domestic trading a touch higher on the day, with the Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  being bolstered by heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In Southeast Asia, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar and Philippine peso were sold down in response to the yuan fears. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht, however, held its own in a day of hectic dealing enlivened by flurries of rumors that the Bank of Thailand was planning to tighten restrictions on domestic banks' baht loans to the offshore market. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 09-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0848GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3901v4m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
