\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Stronger Late Vs Dlr As Yen Moves Higher \b0\par\par\uc2  By Brian Truscott \par \uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1999\par 10:14\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)-- Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were generally stronger against the U.S. dollar in late, choppy trading Thursday, as the yen found new footing against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed heavily on regional markets. \par \par \uc2  Traders in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, Thai baht and yen markets were especially cognizant of central banks, as well as their U.S. dollar-buying agents, keeping close watch on the strength of the respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As the U.S. dollar fell below Y111 and headed toward a key resistance level at Y110, traders wondered aloud when Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would make its presence felt. Japanese politicians and exporters have been voicing concerns about the detrimental effects of a strong yen, leaving the market poised for a massive yen-selling exercise by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "This week has been remarkable in the sense that the majors have been so volatile," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist a U.S. investment bank said. "There are no real themes to be found in the yen, euro and U.S. dollar. Even people who are bearish on the yen aren't really taking positions because market liquidity is poor and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements have been too whippy." \par \par \uc2  As the yen has strengthened, the Singapore dollar has weakened against the U.S. dollar, leaving traders convinced that the republic's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now finally decoupled from the movement of the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The Singapore government is actively supporting the U.S. dollar because the Singapore dollar has room to depreciate," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at a U.K. bank, noting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore let the republic's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slide by 10% in 1986 during the last recession. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  01-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0414EST \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010826dv170017w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
