\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Early On U.S. Dlr Short Covering \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 1998\par 04:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is losing ground to the U.S. dollar in early trading Wednesday, as a wave of U.S. dollar buying sweeps the region. \par \par \uc2  At 0235 GMT (9:35 p.m. Tuesday EST), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.6555, up from S$1.6518 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  There is a growing consensus among traders that the Singapore dollar is no longer moving in a consistent pattern with the yen, as has been the case for most of the year. \par \par \uc2  "There is no correlation, the U.S. dollar has moved from Y124 (last month) to Y116 or so last night, but moved higher against the Singapore dollar," said a trader at a U.S. bank. "The movement now is a function of people being short U.S. dollars and that's now coming off." \par \par \uc2  There has been speculation in the past few months that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been active in the market, either through direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or with the cooperation of the big four domestic banks, but traders said that no longer appears to be the case. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS stopped the U.S. dollar from heading below S$1.60, which is where it should be now, given the strength of the yen," said the trader at the U.S. bank. "The short U.S. dollar market had been positioned on the yen, and that has proven to be incorrect, and people are unwinding their positions." \par \par \uc2  Traders said the U.S. dollar will move between S$1.6530 and S$1.6630 during the session. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight offer rate on the Singapore dollar was 0.75%, up from 0.50% Tuesday. The three-month rate was unchanged 1.875%. \par \par \uc2  -By Brian Truscott; 65 421 4800; btruscott@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-12-98 \par \par \uc2  0305GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917ducg020cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
