\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Range-Bound Late In Asia Despite Weak U.S. Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 1998\par 11:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar remained range-bound against the U.S. dollar throughout Asian trading on Monday, strengthening just a touch against the U.S. dollar, despite the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Despite the U.S. dollar's softness in the major markets, traders shied away from selling it aggressively against the Singapore dollar, afraid that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was poised to enter the market buying U.S. dollars should the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dip below the S$1.6450 level. \par \par \uc2  With few natural sellers of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in evidence, the U.S. dollar just drifted sideways. \par \par \uc2  According to the treasurer of one \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank, however, the market's nervousness at provoking MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not justified. \par \par \uc2  "There is no real (U.S. dollar buying) interest at the moment. I think the market (for the U.S. dollar) will just drift lower," he said, predicting that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will ease towards S$1.6400 through the course of the week. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6470, down from S$1.6490 late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight interbank offer rate on the Singapore dollar is quoted at 0.325%, up from 0.125% earlier. The three-month rate is flat at 1.875%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 