\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -4: Singapore Dollar Drifts Sideways \b0\par\par\uc2 229 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 1998\par 11:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian hours, the U.S. dollar was quoted at 35.7350 baht (THB), up just a fraction from THB35.7250 late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar, meanwhile, remained range-bound against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Despite the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness against the yen, traders shied away from selling the U.S. dollar aggressively against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , afraid that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was poised to enter the market and buy dollars, should the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dip below the S$1.6450 level. \par \par \uc2  With few natural sellers of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in evidence, the U.S. dollar just drifted sideways. \par \par \uc2  According to the treasurer of one \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank, the market's nervousness at provoking MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't justified. \par \par \uc2  "There is no real (U.S. dollar buying) interest at the moment. I think the market (for the U.S. dollar) will just drift lower," he said, predicting that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will ease towards S$1.6400 in the course of the week. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6470, down from S$1.6490 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah (IDR) ended Asian hours flat, with the U.S. dollar unchanged at IDR7,525. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-12-98 \par \par \uc2  1011GMT \