\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Flat Early Despite US$ Weakness Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1998\par 03:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is flat in early trading in Asia Friday, despite the overnight slide in the U.S. dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders attribute the lack of price action in the local market to the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to forestall what it is likely to consider excessive appreciation of the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  Fears that the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will enter the market to buy U.S. dollars at levels around S$1.6400 are supporting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above that level, traders say. \par \par \uc2  At 0200 GMT (9:00 p.m. Thursday EST), the U.S. dollar is trading at S$1.6457, little changed from S$1.6449 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  In the local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated interbank money market, the overnight offered rate on the Singapore dollar is at 1.0%, up from 0.5% late Thursday. The three-month rate is flat at 2.125%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-12-98 \par \par \uc2  0214GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duc401r63\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
