\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Ends Lower In Asia On Local Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1998\par 12:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar finished Asian hours lower Wednesday, after U.S. dollar-buying from local banks in early trading wiped out the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight gains. \par \par \uc2  After London clearing banks sold down the U.S. dollar during European hours Tuesday, traders reported that Singapore banks were aggressively bidding up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trading Wednesday, leading some to suspect that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was behind the buying. \par \par \uc2  Like other central banks around the region, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely believed to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to safeguard domestic export competitiveness by moderating any tendency the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to appreciate. \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday in Asia, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6506, up from S$1.6471 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated interbank money market, the overnight offer rate on the Singapore dollar is 0.125%, the same as late Tuesday. The three-month rate is also flat at 2.125%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-12-98 \par \par \uc2  1117GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duc201ocz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley1