\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Driven Down Early By Local Bank Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1998\par 03:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar has dropped sharply in early trading, sold down by the domestic banks, according to traders. \par \par \uc2  "The local banks are buying (U.S. dollars) aggressively," said a trader at a U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "The U.K. clearing banks were selling the U.S. dollar down in London hours, and it looks like the authority is pretty keen to bring it back up," he explained, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, which is widely believed in the market to be behind the move. \par \par \uc2  The de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which manages monetary policy in Singapore using its ample reserves actively to steer the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's exchange rate, is widely believed to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to guard \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness by moderating any tendency the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to appreciate. \par \par \uc2  After the buying pressure earlier brushed aside interest to sell U.S. dollars at around S$1.6500, many traders are anticipating a rapid move up to test resistance at S$1.6600. \par \par \uc2  At 0215 GMT (9:15 p.m. EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6530, up from S$1.6471 late in Asia on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -denominated interbank money market, the\par overnight offer rate on the Singapore dollar is 0.75%, up from 0.125%\par late the previous day. The three-month rate is flat at 2.125%.\par    