\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -4: Investor Confidence In Baht Dented \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1998\par 11:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Despite the widespread optimism, serious concerns cloud the baht's outlook. Many analysts point to the failure of Thailand's sixth letter of intent to the IMF, signed on Tuesday, to incorporate an expected commitment to introduce a comprehensive bankruptcy law. The success of Thailand's opposition parties in blocking the measure has severely dented investor confidence, they say. \par \par \uc2  Among other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Singapore dollar finished Asian trading hours lower, after aggressive U.S. dollar buying from local banks wiped out the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight gains in early trading. \par \par \uc2  Like other central banks around the region, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely believed to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to safeguard domestic export competitiveness by moderating any tendency the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to appreciate. \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday in Asia, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6506, up from S$1.6471 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the rupiah (IDR), the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at IDR7,472, barely different from IDR7,465 Tuesday as political risk concerns kept the market sidelined. \par \par \uc2  In North Asian markets, the U.S. dollar slipped moderately, in parallel with a fall against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Against the new Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended domestic trading at NT$32.420, down from NT$32.438 the previous day. Against the South Korean won (KRW), the U.S. dollar ended at KRW1,238, down from KRW1,245 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-12-98 \par \par \uc2  1057GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duc201o8w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
