\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late But Export Data Sours Sentiment \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 1998\par 12:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Although the Singapore dollar ended Asian trading hours on Friday a touch higher against the U.S. dollar, a sharp fall in Singapore's non-oil domestic exports - a key leading indicator of economic performance - damped sentiment towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  After October's non-oil domestic exports registered a 4.8% year-on-year decline, significantly worse than economists' consensus expectations of a 0.68% fall, most traders argued that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has little leeway to strengthen in the near future. \par \par \uc2  "The Singapore economy is in a position where a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't help. Logically the Singapore dollar should be weaker, and I think the government will help that," said the managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at one U.S. investment bank in Singapore, implying that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to head off further local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "I can't see the dollar/Sing coming much below S$1.62," agreed a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Singapore bank, employing market shorthand for the U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar exchange rate. Further local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation would threaten to undermine Singapore's economic competitiveness, he said. \par \par \uc2  Late Friday the U.S. dollar ended Asian interbank trading hours at S$1.6290, down slightly from S$1.6315 the previous day. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight interbank offered rate on the Singapore dollar was quoted at 1.00% late Friday, up a touch from 1.25% the previous evening. At 2.25%, down from 2.375%, the three-month rate was slightly lower. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-11-98 \par \par \uc2  1124GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dubk01d6h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
