\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Higher Early, Fueled By Yen's Rise Vs US$ \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 1998\par 03:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is substantially stronger against the U.S. dollar early Friday than it was late in Asia on Thursday, as the overnight rally in the Japanese yen has boosted the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But although the yen's rise following Thursday's formation of a coalition pact between Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party and the opposition Liberal Party has helped to fuel the Singapore dollar's rally, traders question the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's potential to make further gains in the short term. \par \par \uc2  "The regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have come up to levels where the central banks do not want see their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  any stronger, in case it jeopardizes economic recovery," said a senior treasury executive at one of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's big four banks. \par \par \uc2  Fearful of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is widely believed to be guarding against any loss of export competitiveness caused by relative appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders are reluctant to sell the U.S. dollar down through the S$1.6200 level. \par \par \uc2  Although most dealers believe the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will encounter strong support between S$1.6180 and S$1.6200, some argue that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sink lower, should it continue to slide against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It's all the yen-effect. I think we will still see the U.S. dollar lower," said a Singapore dollar trader at a German bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0225 GMT (9:25 p.m. Thursday EST) the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6218, down steeply from S$1.6310 late in Asian trading the previous day. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight interbank offer rate on the Singapore dollar is quoted at 1.25%, unchanged from the previous evening. At 2.375%, the three-month rate is also flat. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-11-98 \par \par \uc2  0241GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dubk01ccv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
