\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Stronger Early, Lifted By Yen Rally \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 1998\par 03:09\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have strengthened sharply against the U.S. dollar in early trading on Friday morning, pulled up by the steep overnight rally in the Japanese yen and by rising local stock markets. \par \par \uc2  But although the yen's rise following Thursday's formation of a coalition pact between Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party and the opposition Liberal Party has helped propel other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher, traders question whether Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make further gains in the short term. \par \par \uc2  "The regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have come up to levels where the central banks do not want see their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  any stronger, in case it jeopardizes economic recovery," said a senior treasury executive at one of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's big four banks. \par \par \uc2  Fearful of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is widely believed to be guarding against any loss of export competitiveness through relative appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders are reluctant to push the U.S. dollar down through the S$1.6200 level. \par \par \uc2  Although most dealers believe the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will encounter strong support between S$1.6180 and S$1.6200, some argue that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sink lower, should it continue to slide against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It's all the yen-effect. I think we will still see the U.S. dollar lower," said a Singapore dollar trader at a German bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0200 GMT (9 p.m. Thursday EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6215, down steeply from S$1.6310 late in Asian trading the previous day. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  11-19-98 \par \par \uc2  2109EST \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916dubk02p9i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
