\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Flat Early, Seen Trading In Narrow Range \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 1998\par 03:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is flat against the U.S. dollar in lackluster, range-bound trading early Friday, with one trader at a German bank in Singapore reporting "a total lack of interest in the market." \par \par \uc2  "There are some commercially driven flows in the Singapore dollar," he said. "But there are no more big speculative plays," he said. \par \par \uc2  Most market participants expect the Singapore dollar to remain confined in a tight S$1.6220 to S$1.6250 range through the course of Asian trading, unless the U.S. dollar should break decisively out of its current Y115 to Y120 range against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The Singapore dollar isn't going anywhere," said another trader, explaining that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is finding support from fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the U.S. dollar dip towards S$1.6200. At the same time, he said, the U.S. dollar is being capped by moderate fund inflows as investor sentiment toward the regional markets brightens. \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT (9 p.m. EST) the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6237, barely changed from S$1.6239 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight offer rate on the Singapore dollar is quoted at 2.00%, up from 1.00% late the previous day. The three-month rate has also edged higher, rising to 2.50% from 2.25%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-11-98 \par \par \uc2 