\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Singapore Dlr Up Early; THB, IDR Steady \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 1998\par 02:53\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Although the Singapore dollar has risen sharply in response to a run-up in the yen, early trading in Southeast Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Monday has left the baht and the rupiah little affected by Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  As the U.S. dollar tumbled through support at Y115 in early Asian trading, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also dipped below S$1.62 against the Singapore dollar, which was boosted by a sharp 2% rise in the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's potential downside against the Singapore dollar is likely to be limited in the short term, however, according to the head of trading at a Singapore bank, who says the U.S. dollar should find support below current levels. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think we will see support at S$1.6150 broken," he said, adding that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to trade in a S$1.6160 to S$1.6250 range through Asian hours on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Although it has strengthened over recent sessions, the Singapore dollar has failed to keep pace with the rally in the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say traders, has been held down by U.S. dollar bids from Singapore banks, leading to strong suspicions that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the republic's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to check the appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0145 GMT (8:45 p.m. Sunday EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6195, down from S$1.6255 in late Asian trading on Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  11-01-98 \par \par \uc2  2053EST \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916dub202ixk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
