\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Higher Early On Yen, Stock Mkt Rally \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 1998\par 02:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar has strengthened in early trading Monday morning in response to a sharp rise in the value of the yen against the U.S. dollar, and a steep 1.9% run-up in the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside is likely to be limited in the short term, however, according to the head of trading at a Singapore bank, who says the U.S. dollar should find support below current levels. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think we will see support at S$1.6150 broken," he said, adding that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to trade in a S$1.6160-.6250 range through Asian hours on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Although it has strengthened over recent sessions, the Singapore dollar has failed to keep pace with the rally in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say traders, has been held down by U.S. dollar bids from Singapore banks, leading to strong suspicions that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the republic's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to check the appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0135 GMT (8:35 p.m. Sunday EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6190, down from S$1.6255 in late Asian trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight interbank offered rate is quoted at 1.25%, compared with 0.75% late on Friday. The three-month rate is at 2.625%, up a touch from 2.125%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-11-98 \par \par \uc2  0145GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dub200opz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
