\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Higher Early; Little Impact From PM's Comments \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 1998\par 03:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar has inched marginally higher in early trading on Thursday, with comments by Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong, who said that the economy shrank by 1.5% in the third quarter, having little impact on the market. \par \par \uc2  Trading is generally subdued, according to dealers, with the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely to remain range-bound despite the grim economic news, according to a trader at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Most market participants have long resigned themselves to the prospect that Singapore will enter a technical recession in the second half of 1998, and official confirmation is not expected to move the market significantly. \par \par \uc2  With profit-takers expected to cap the U.S. dollar's upside around S$1.6350, and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  supporting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at S$1.6200, few expect the market to break out of that range, said the local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  At 0210 GMT (9:10 p.m. Wednesday EST), the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6232, down fractionally from S$1.6235 toward the end of Asian trading the day before. \par \par \uc2  In the local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight interbank offered rate is quoted at 1.25%, up from 0.0625% late the previous day. The three-month rate is unchanged at 2.75%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0217GMT \par \par \uc2  116