\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Lower Late But Some See US$ Dn To S$1.60 \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 1998\par 14:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar slipped back in Asian trading on Friday from levels seen at the height of the yen's rebound against the U.S. dollar on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Despite the slight easing, however, analysts and traders warn that the Singapore dollar's rally - generally attributed to U.S.-dollar sales by hedge funds forced to unwind positions as banks trim credit lines - may continue into the coming week. \par \par \uc2  Despite the enormous volume of long-U.S. dollar positions liquidated over recent weeks, traders warn that the unwinding has not yet run its course. \par \par \uc2  With investment banks continuing to sell U.S. dollars on Friday, traders say the upward pressure on the Singapore dollar may push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down, to test S$1.60 in the coming week, especially if the yen's rally continues. \par \par \uc2  If that does happen, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, buying U.S. dollars order to check the rise of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say traders. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS has been on the bid at every level, all the way down from S$1.67," said a Singapore-dollar trader at a U.S. bank, saying that the authority has been active over the past week. \par \par \uc2  As Asian trading drew to a close on Friday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6491, a touch stronger than S$1.6344 late on Thursday, but down steeply from S$1.6885 a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight interbank offered rate on the Singapore dollar was at 0.75%, up from 0.125% the previous day. The three-month rate was unchanged, at 3.875%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1202GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dua9001va\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
