\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Up Early On  \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority \highlight\uc2  Stance \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 1998\par 05:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is stronger against the U.S. dollar in early morning trading on Tuesday, following comments Monday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have assuaged investors' fears of immediate government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The MAS said it is taking a flexible position with regard to the exchange rate, meaning the dollar/sing (value of the U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar) will remain firm and gradually move higher," one trader at a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  Other traders said the Singapore dollar will continue to track the fortunes of the dollar-yen. Japaneses Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa hinted Tuesday morning that government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't look imminent as long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are not disruptive, which he said is the case at the moment. \par \par \uc2  His comments immediately pushed the U.S. dollar higher against the yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "That will put some downward pressure on the Singapore dollar, and after the MAS comments, the market might start selling Singapore dollars against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the Malaysian ringgit," said one trader at a French bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0310 GMT (11:10 p.m. Monday EDT), the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.7654, down from S$1.7677 in late trading in Asia Monday. In the cross markets, the ringgit was stronger against the Singapore dollar at S$O.4213 in early trading, up from S$0.4191 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  money market, the overnight interbank rate is\par offered at 3%, up from Monday's rate of 0.125%. The three-month rate is\par offered at 4.25%, down from 5%.\par    -By Brian Truscott; 65 421 4800; btruscott@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 25-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0329GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8p077lt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
