\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Edge Higher; Outlook Remains Stormy \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 11:52\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  edged a\par touch higher during Asian trading hours on Friday, in tandem\par with the yen and regional stock markets.\par    As lingering fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lifted\par the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the U.S. dollar, participants\par in the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets pared back their\par long positions in the U.S. dollar in the run-up to the\par weekend.\par    But although analysts and traders say that trading over\par the coming week will be choppy, warning that the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is highly vulnerable to a short-term correction,\par most maintain the view that the U.S. dollar remains a\par long-term buy against Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    "What we could see is weak dollar longs squeezed out as\par short-term events drive people out of their positions," said\par Jonathan Hazell, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Barclays\par Capital in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    While either yen-supportive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the bank of\par Japan or any further drops in the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  stock market are\par likely to trigger flurries of U.S. dollar selling in the\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, the boost to Southeast\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be short-lived argue market observers.\par    "At the moment term regional markets are being driven by\par short-term speculative plays. People are buying and selling\par in ranges as fresh concerns emerge," says Thio Chin Loo,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Banque Paribas in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    "If we do see \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the yen, players will take\par profits from their long dollar positions against the Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and then look to buy the dollar on dips," she\par predicted.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  08-14-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0552EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8e01xr0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
