\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Rallies On Yen, But Still Seen As A Sell \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 13:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rallied sharply against the U.S, dollar during Asian trading on Wednesday, trailing the rebound in the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  After opening up sharply against the U.S. dollar, as early profit-taking triggered a massive surge in the yen, the Singapore dollar drifted higher still over the rest of a trading session dominated by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The whole market is long U.S. dollars, so people would rather take profits than risk getting caught on the wrong side of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," explained one \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 -based trader of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian trading the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had fallen to S$1.7454, down from S$1.7595 late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Although any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the yen would inevitably bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, too, the mood in the market remains profoundly bearish. \par \par \uc2  "People are still looking to buy dollars," said the head of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at a U.K. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  After the Singapore trade minister on Tuesday expressed concern at the impact on competitiveness of the Singapore dollar's appreciation relative to other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , many market participants are convinced the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to drop. \par \par \uc2  "Selling the Singapore dollar is an even better bet then selling yen right now," said the U.K. bank trading chief. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the ringgit ended at S$0.4165, up from S$0.4133, towards the end of Asian trading on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight interbank rate was quoted at 0.00%%-0.125%, down from 0.625% late the previous day. The three-month rate was at 4.875%-5.125, down from 5.125% to 5.375%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1134GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8c06vec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
