\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Rebound As Yen Rally Relieves Pressure \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 11:56\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The rebound of Japan's yen from\par Tuesday's eight-year low relieved the downward pressure on\par Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which rallied across the board\par during Asian trading hours on Wednesday.\par    After opening up sharply against the U.S. dollar as early\par profit-taking triggered a massive surge in the yen, Southeast\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drifted higher still over the rest of a\par trading session dominated by fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    "The whole market is long U.S. dollars, so people would\par rather take profits than risk getting caught on the wrong\par side of any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," explained one \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -based\par trader of regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Although any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost the yen would\par inevitably bolster Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as well, the\par mood in the market remains profoundly bearish toward regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the longer term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "People are still looking to buy dollars," said the head\par of regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at a U.K. bank in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "If\par there is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , they will shy away from the market for\par the time being. But at the end of the day \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does\par not strengthen banking systems or reduce levels of\par non-performing loans, so the market may just take\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a good opportunity to buy," U.S. dollars\par against the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    In the short to medium term, however, few participants\par foresee any decoupling of Asian markets, most predicting that\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to shadow the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  08-12-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0556EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8c01v77\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
