\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up With Yen, Singapore Dlr Bucks Trend \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1998\par 04:22\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht and Malaysian\par ringgit rose early Wednesday on the back of overnight gains\par in the yen, but the Singapore dollar fell on what dealers are\par ascribing to possible U.S. dollar purchases by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore.\par    "I'm not really sure why the Singapore dollar is falling\par - you would have to ask the local banks about that," said a\par trader at a U.S. bank in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    When the MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, it frequently does\par so through local banks, dealers say.\par    An MAS official said that the authority has a policy\par never to comment on open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    "The Singapore dollar's behavior is a bit strange this\par morning," said a trader at a local bank. "The U.S. dollar\par should be lower today, but it was oversold yesterday."\par    The local bank trader did note big demand for U.S.\par dollars, but would not specify where it was coming from.\par    At 0215 GMT (10:15 p.m. Tuesday EDT), the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar is\par quoted at S$1.7139, up from S$1.7122 late Tuesday in Asia.\par    Dealers say volume was thin in other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par although there was some interest in the market to sell\par dollars for Indonesian rupiah.\par    Traders are awaiting the annual meeting of the\par Consultative Group on Indonesia later Wednesday in Paris. The\par CGI is a group of countries that serve as international\par lenders to Indonesia.\par    Market participants expect that Indonesia will receive\par significantly more than the US$5.3 billion the group pledged\par last year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  07-28-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2222EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du7t01s9w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
