\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Up Late In Narrow Trade;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rumored \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1998\par 12:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is slightly higher late Wednesday in choppy, rangebound trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say market rumors of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore buying U.S. dollars at S$1.71 put a floor under the U.S. dollar, which was suffering globally on the political problems of U.S. President Bill Clinton. \par \par \uc2  An MAS official said the authority has a policy never to comment on open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after news broke that former White House intern Monica Lewinsky will testify before a grand jury about her relationship with the president. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a local bank in Singapore said U.S. investors were seen early in the market selling U.S. dollars around S$1.7175 before the MAS rumors broke, driving the dollar back down. \par \par \uc2  "Singapore people were buying dollars on the back of B.G. Lee's statement that Singapore is losing competitiveness due to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements," said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Later, investors out of London also showed interest to sell dollars in the afternoon, but dealers say talk of continuing MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ensured the U.S. dollar didn't fall below S$1.71 before interbank trading ended in Asia. \par \par \uc2  At 1005 GMT (6:05 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.7090, down from S$1.7122 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is at S$0.4178, up from S$0.4150 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 1.00%-1.50%, up from 0.50%-1.00% in Asian dealing Tuesday. The three-month rate is at 5.25%-5.50%, unchanged from Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Robert Quist; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-07-98 \par \par \uc2  1015GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7t06f6j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
