\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Down Early, Rumors of MAS Buying U.S. Dlrs \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1998\par 03:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is lower early Wednesday despite gains made overnight by the Japanese yen, which the Singapore dollar has been tracking closely for several weeks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore say there is a strong possibility that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, the island republic's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was in the market buying U.S. dollars Wednesday morning. \par \par \uc2  An MAS official said that the authority has a policy never to comment on open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I'm not really sure why the Singapore dollar is falling - you would have to ask the local banks about that," said a trader at a U.S. bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  When the MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, it frequently does so through local banks, dealers say. \par \par \uc2  "The Singapore dollar's behavior is a bit strange this morning," said a trader at a local bank. "The U.S. dollar should be lower today, but it was oversold yesterday." \par \par \uc2  The local bank trader did note big demand for U.S. dollars, but would not specify where it was coming from. \par \par \uc2  A trader at another U.S. bank said there was some market talk that the MAS had been in the market earlier this week and last week, as well, pressuring the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  At 0145 GMT (9:45 p.m. Tuesday EDT), the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.7132, up from S$1.7122 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is at S$0.4164, up from S$0.4150 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 1.00%-1.50%, up from 0.50%-1.00% in Asian dealing Tuesday. The three-month rate is at 5.25%-5.50%, unchanged from Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Robert Quist; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0151GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7t06d2z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
