\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Early Vs U.S. Dlr, Ringgit, Shadowing Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1998\par 05:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is higher in mid-morning trading on Wednesday after strengthening overnight and early Wednesday in line with a rally with the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  The rise in the yen was triggered by further hints from Japanese officials that the ruling Liberal Democratic Party is leaning in favor of introducing permanent tax cuts. \par \par \uc2  Although the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has proved the most sensitive of the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to yen rallies, traders say underlying sentiment remains bleak after Singapore Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong warned yesterday that Singapore may face recession in 1999. \par \par \uc2  At 0330 GMT (11:30 p.m. EDT) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6990, down from S$1.7100 in late trading the day before. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has also risen against the ringgit with market participants reporting interest to sell the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in both Singapore and Hong Kong also say, however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around S$0.4000 to check what it regards as excess appreciation of the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently quoted at S$0.4088, down from S$0.4133 late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits has risen to 5.00%-5.50% from 0.0.125%-0.25% late on Tuesday. The three-month rate has edged higher to 6.25%-6.50% from 5.75%-6.25%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0344GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7805rvr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
