\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore MAS: Mkt Forces Will Determine S$ Value - Report \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 1998\par 08:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, or MAS, will continue to allow market forces to determine the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, but will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter unwarranted speculation, according to a report in the Business Times' weekend edition. \par \par \uc2  The MAS, which is Singapore's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the value of the Singapore dollar is determined by market forces, and at the same time, by maintaining a trade-weighted exchange band, according to the article. (US$1=S$1.6210) \par \par \uc2  The article quoted an MAS official as saying: "We manage the exchange rate against a basket of trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of our major trading partners, because that's the best way to preserve our purchasing power. We allow a band within which the trade-weighted exchange rate can fluctuate." \par \par \uc2  The MAS' policy goal is to achieve sustained non-inflationary growth, the article said. \par \par \uc2  Even if the exchange rate moves out of the band, the MAS official said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't be automatic, the article said. \par \par \uc2  The band is adjusted according to how the MAS perceives inflation, adding that as long as the exchange rate stays within the band, the MAS wouldn't influence it, the article added. \par \par \uc2  The MAS will only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar if the exchange rate moves too sharply because of unwarranted speculation or if its movement is inconsistent with MAS' view of the fundamentals, the article said. \par \par \uc2  The article quoted the MAS official as saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "if the outlook for the region suddenly worsens. It's not our job to support what is not sustainable on a fundamental basis." \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  20-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0646GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010914du6k00l66\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
