\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late On Yen Rally; MAS Rumors Brake Gains \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 13:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar made dramatic gains against the U.S. dollar Thursday, spurred on by joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar/yen market by the U.S. and Japan overnight. \par \par \uc2  However, rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in the morning by buying U.S. dollars at S$1.6550 effectively put a lid on Singapore dollar bullishness, according to Thio Chin Loo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Banque Paribas in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  A trader with a Japanese bank in Singapore said market players were spooked when they saw a big local bank buying U.S. dollars. "Some rushed to buy U.S. dollars after they saw that," he said. \par \par \uc2  However, a trader at a domestic bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  expressed doubt that the MAS had actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It was probably a commercial buyer," the trader said. "The market is very nervous and it looks cheap right now for corporates to buy U.S. dollars." \par \par \uc2  Traders also cited political uncertainties in Indonesia and Malaysia as reasons to buy the U.S. dollar against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1105 GMT, the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6605, up from an early low of S$1.6400, but well down from S$1.7190 late Wednesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit is lower at S$0.4210, compared with S$0.4247 late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate on Singapore dollar-denominated deposits is currently quoted at 5.00%-5.50%, down from 6.00%-6.50% late the previous day. The three-month rate is at 6.00%-6.50%, down from 6.25%-6.75% on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Robert Quist; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1120GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6i056r2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
