\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: MAS Rumors Rein In Singapore Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 12:51\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The rest of the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tracked the yen much\par more closely.\par    "Obviously, the Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be very\par much biased by what happens with dollar/yen, but in the\par absence of big shocks in that market, the regionals will tend\par to drift weaker," Fung said.\par    "The weak yen was an exacerbating factor in regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness, but it was not the fundamental cause, and\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hasn't changed that fact," he said. "The outlook\par for recessions in the region hasn't changed, so I don't see\par why anyone would be aggressively bullish on the regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the moment."\par    In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , rumors that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market in the morning by\par buying U.S. dollars at S$1.6550 effectively put a lid on\par Singapore dollar bullishness, according to Thio with\par Paribas.\par    A trader at a domestic bank in Singapore said there were\par big U.S. dollar buyers in the market, but expressed doubt\par that the MAS had actually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "It was probably a commercial buyer," the trader said.\par "The market is very nervous and it looks cheap right now for\par corporates to buy U.S. dollars."\par    Traders also cited political uncertainties in Indonesia\par and Malaysia as reasons to buy the U.S. dollar against the\par Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    At 1035 GMT, the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6590, up\par from an early low of S$1.6400, but well down from S$1.7190\par late Wednesday in Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  06-18-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0651EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du6i01k39\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
