\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore growth seen hurt by Asia economic woes. \b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 1998\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 16 (Reuters) - Singapore's economic growth is expected to slip more than forecast because of Asia's economic crisis and could contract if the turmoil got worse, an official of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "We're in the process of reviewing the growth rates for the year," Khor Hoe Ee said. \par \par \uc2  Khor, director of the economics department at the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told a seminar that a review of Singapore's 1998 growth forecast was expected to show a smaller rate of growth for 1998 than the current official projection of 2.5 to 4.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "We expect that we'll come out at the lower end of that range. If we're lucky we'll stay there," he said. \par \par \uc2  Several economists have said that Singapore faced a likely recession due to the regional crisis. Even those who are more optimistic feel the official forecast is too high. \par \par \uc2  "If the external environment became more adverse, then I think it's not unfair to say the economy could dip into negative," Khor added. \par \par \uc2  But he said there was confidence about the soundness of the economy and some sectors were still faring well. \par \par \uc2  If the Japanese economy revived and the European economy continued to strengthen, boosting Singapore exports, there was a fair chance Singapore's economy would turn around, he said. \par \par \uc2  Despite the economic slowdown, there were still pockets of strength, such as in growth of semiconductors. \par \par \uc2  Electronics account for about 70 percent of Singapore's non-oil exports. \par \par \uc2  Further, the government's promise to stimulate the economy with off-budget measures if second quarter figures showed significant decline would also help alleviate problems. \par \par \uc2  He said off-budget measures could be announced around the time the economic review was finalised. That is expected within a month. \par \par \uc2  Asked what kind of reserves \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had used during the recent financial turmoil, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, he said: "Like all central banks we do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but our attention has been directed at smoothing out the volatility." \par \par \uc2  He said the Singapore dollar's exchange rate depended on market conditions. \par \par \uc2  "We operate flexibly, I would say, with a band in which we allow the exchange rate to fluctuate. And as long as it fluctuates within that band, we don't really \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  However, it was unrealistic for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar to remain high when regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were weakening, he said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar exchange rate is managed against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has fallen around 18 percent against the U.S. dollar since the start of Asia's crisis a year ago. \par \par \uc2  "We believe our fundamentals are a lot stronger than most countries. The underlying tendency for the exchange rate is to appreciate over time rather than depreciate," Khor said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6g02uud\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
