\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Late-AM -2: Mkt Split On Chance Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1998\par 06:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Although few market participants doubt that the dollar is set to go higher, with many longer term-players not looking to take profits until Y145 is reached, the run-up will be slow and difficult, they say. \par \par \uc2  "Some profit-taking dollar selling will appear at Y142.20 to Y142.30, which will slow the movement," said the Japanese bank senior trader, adding, however, that Japanese investors, poised to buy the dollar on dips will continue to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders remain divided over the prospect of joint G-7 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reverse the yen's slide. While some argue that the Federal Reserve and European central banks would be unwilling to commit reserves to shoring up the yen without evidence of effective economic reform in Japan, others maintain that the catastrophic effects on the rest of Asia of further yen depreciation will force the G-7's hand. \par \par \uc2  Most traders agree, however, that the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan acting alone would be limited. \par \par \uc2  "If the Bank of Japan starts to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it will ask the G-7 central banks to contribute, otherwise the effectiveness will be very small," said the Japanese bank's senior dealer. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar is little changed against the Deutsche mark, trading at DEM1.7965, down a touch from DEM1.7970 earlier in Tokyo but above DEM1.7955 late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, the mark is higher against the yen, trading up to Y78.95 from Y78.90 earlier in Tokyo and Y78.80 in New York late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0411GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6b050gc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
