\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dollar level dictated by market - Hu. \b0\par\par\uc2 139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 1998\par 11:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 2 (Reuters) - Singapore Finance Minister Richard Hu said on Tuesday the level of the Singapore dollar was decided by the market. \par \par \uc2  "We don't defend the Singapore dollar. The Singapore dollar level is market-dictated," Hu told reporters on the sidelines of a news conference launching a new bank product. \par \par \uc2  He said the "MAS (\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) only goes in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid large fluctuations". \par \par \uc2  "No one can successfully defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at unrealistic levels indefinitely," Hu said. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether Singapore exports, which are showing signs of slowing, could influence the government's idea of where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate should be, Hu said: "That has never been an issue." \par \par \uc2  - Singapore Newsroom (65) 870-3080; Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  - Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6203st4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
