\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 -4: Ctrl Bks Seen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  In Forwards \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1998\par 15:31\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Although most traders believe that regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par are set to drop further against the dollar, some argue that\par they will be supported by high offshore interest rates,\par which make the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  uncomfortably expensive to sell\par short.\par    "It will take some doing to keep the dollar above\par THB40," said one local bank trader. "People will buy baht\par because the interest rates are so high."\par    The baht interest rate implied by the offshore one month\par U.S. dollar/baht swap offer rate edged higher to 38% on\par Friday, up from 36% a day earlier.\par    The local bank trader said that investors would find such\par high yields irresistible, particularly if a portion of the\par exchange rate risk can be hedged out by going long on the\par baht against a short position in the Singapore dollar, which\par late on Friday was yielding only around 8%.\par    "A 20% yield differential is very attractive," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Similar opportunities exist for the ringgit, which late\par Friday offered a one month offshore implied interest rate of\par 26%.\par    While restricted liquidity in offshore markets is keeping\par implied interest rates high, some traders and analysts\par maintain that offshore rates are being artificially\par bolstered as a deterrent to speculators.\par    "Central banks are \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the forward markets to\par bid up forward rates," said one \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -based analyst at a\par European bank.\par    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through the forward market is a classic\par means for a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to attempt to deter speculation\par against its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Higher forward rates mean a higher\par offshore interest rate, which increases the cost of funding\par for market participants looking to sell a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  short.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  05-29-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0931EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du5t01eax\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
