\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Falls Early On Weak Yen, Economy Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1998\par 04:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is down against the U.S. dollar early Wednesday on the weak yen and suggestions from government officials that the Singapore economy may be slowing. \par \par \uc2  However, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide is capped somewhat by concerns in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) may step into the market to support the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  At 0230 GMT (10:30 p.m. Tuesday EDT) the U.S. dollar is trading at S$1.6565, up from S$1.6524 quoted late in Asian hours on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a local bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  says dealers are worried about the possibility of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  above S$1.6600. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. dollar will remain firm fundamentally, but trading is cautious because of concerns over MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he says. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit is quoted at S$0.4322 at 0235 GMT, down slightly from S$0.4325 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's domestic money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar-denominated deposits has eased to 1.50%-1.625%, down from 1.875%-2.00% late on Tuesday. The three-month rate is little changed at 5.625%-5.875% from 5.75%-6.00% late the day before. \par \par \uc2  -By Robert Quist; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0246GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5r04ia3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwg