\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Late-AM -2: BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Considered Futile \b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 1998\par 05:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  With such a weight of demand propelling both the dollar and the mark higher against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders believe the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan is small despite repeated warnings that the Japanese authorities will act to correct what they regard as excessive yen weakness. \par \par \uc2  The chances of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in conjunction with the U.S. Federal Reserve is regarded as remote, following weekend reports that U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin is prepared to see the dollar rise to levels as high as Y150, if that would help support the Japanese economy by boosting exports. \par \par \uc2  "Rubin had the opportunity to deny the reports on Sunday, and he didn't. All he did was reiterate the U.S.'s strong dollar policy," said the German bank trader. "So the risk is to the dollar's upside." \par \par \uc2  With the chances of concerted action diminished, traders doubt the likely effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan alone. \par \par \uc2  "Considering the current market conditions, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have limited impact. The BOJ will wait for more favorable conditions," said the Japanese bank trader, recalling recent statements that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would rather \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reinforce a yen rally than act to check its fall. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, activity in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is relatively subdued. Against the mark, the dollar is at DEM1.7625, down a touch from DEM1.7635 earlier in Tokyo and below DEM1.7650 late Monday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6298, little changed from $1.6297 earlier in Tokyo but above $1.6275 in Europe late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0356GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5q04gig\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
