\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Late-AM: U.S. Dlr Lower; Fear Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 1998\par 06:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The dollar is marginally lower in late-morning Singapore trading Monday from levels around 0210 GMT in Tokyo with short-term movements, especially in the yen, likely to be dictated by developments in Indonesia and the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Basically people are keen on pushing the dollar (versus the yen) higher but people are also paralyzed with fear by (the prospect) of the Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," said a dealer with a major U.K. bank here. \par \par \uc2  "The yen will definitely be affected by what happens to (Indonesian President) Suharto. Will Suharto go or will he stay? People want to know that," said the treasurer at a major Australian bank here. Movements in the rupiah should have a spill-over impact on the yen, he said. \par \par \uc2  Although at least one Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling the dollar against the yen near the intraday high of Y136.05, several U.S. and Swiss brokerages are keen on buying dollars at Y135.80-.85, said market players. \par \par \uc2  Market players expect the dollar to stay largely range-bound against the mark amid a lack of fresh developments in Asian trading. The dollar is expected to hold between DEM1.7820 and DEM1.7860, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  Around 0330 GMT, the dollar is at Y135.90, slightly down from Y136.04 around 0210 GMT, and from Y136.27 late Monday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at DEM1.7850, down from DEM1.7856 and from DEM1.7860 in New York Monday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6235, up from $1.6221 at 0210 GMT and from $1.6220 late Monday in New York. The mark is quoted at Y76.16, a touch lower than Y76.19 at 0210 GMT and Y76.30 in New York late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Joseph Rajendran; 65 421 4800. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0400GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5j047x0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
