\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Up Early, But Seen Testing Downside Again \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1998\par 05:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is stronger against the U.S. dollar in early trading on Thursday, compared with levels seen late Wednesday and in overnight trading. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently looking bid, however, and traders are predicting that the Singapore dollar will weaken from its present level in the immediate near term. \par \par \uc2  After falling in line with Wednesday's drop in the Indonesian rupiah triggered by anti-government riots in Jakarta, the Singapore dollar opened Asian trading on Thursday up from its overnight lows. The rise came as market participants took profits in response to a report in the Jakarta Post indicating that Indonesia's President Suharto may be prepared to retire, said traders. \par \par \uc2  "The only thing I can say is that everything depends on what happens in Jakarta," said a senior treasury executive at a Singapore bank. "At the moment it looks like the correction is over and we may see the U.S. dollar test higher." \par \par \uc2  At 0255 GMT (10:55 p.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6485, up a touch from its earlier intraday low of S$1.6425, but still well below S$1.6549 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Levels around S$1.6520 should provide a cap for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term, say traders. \par \par \uc2  Should the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade much higher, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check its rise, say traders. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 5.75%-6.00%, compared with 6.00%-6.25% late on Wednesday. The three-month rate is higher at 7.00%-7.50% from 6.75%-7.00%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0318GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5e04275\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
