\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Ends Down, But Up From Intraday Low \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1998\par 14:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar ended Asian trading hours steeply lower on Thursday, although up from its intraday low. \par \par \uc2  In early trading the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plummeted against the U.S. dollar in line with a sharp sell-off in the other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  After breaking up though S$1.6000 in European hours on Wednesday, the U.S. dollar surged to hit a high of S$1.6410 early Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's rise against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spurred by warnings from chairman Seng Wee that Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp. may need to make 'further substantial provisions' in 1998 given the bleak economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar fell back from its high, however, on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a liquidity squeeze, which also saw the U.S. dollar retreat against other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6215, up sharply from S$1.5997 a day previously. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was at S$0.4194, down from S$0.4216 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's domestic money market, the overnight rate on local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits eased to 3.00%-3.25% from 5.00%-5.50% earlier. Late Wednesday it was at 2.00%-2.50%. The three-month rate has risen to 5.50%-6.00% unchanged from earlier but up from 5.125%-5.25% the previous day. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-05-98 \par \par \uc2  1202GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 4254 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5703v8h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
