\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -3: Liquidity Squeeze Halts Slide \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1998\par 13:19\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Worried that the Bank of Thailand would defend the baht\par by refusing to roll over maturing swap contracts dating from\par the attack on the baht a year ago - further squeezing market\par participants running short positions in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -\par traders rushed to acquire baht, pushing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher\par again.\par    By late in Asian trading the U.S. dollar had dropped to\par THB38.6750, just a touch higher than THB38.6050 late on\par Wednesday.\par    The effect of the liquidity squeeze was augmented by\par market talk that both Bank Negara and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were heard checking rates, the normal precursor\par to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Within hours the ringgit had recovered most of the ground\par lost earlier, while the Singapore dollar also strengthened.\par    Late in Asia the U.S. dollar was at MYR3.8625, up from\par MYR3.7925 late the day before. The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also at\par S$1.6260, off its earlier high, but still up sharply from\par S$1.5997 the day before.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Only the rupiah failed to rebound convincingly from its\par intraday low, although it did claw back some territory, aided\par by the news, leaked well in advance, that Bank Indonesia was\par to raise short-term interest rates a further notch.\par    When the raise came, which boosted the rate on one-month\par Sertifikat Bank Indonesia notes to 58% from 50%, it was\par dismissed by the market as inadequate.\par    "An interest rate rise at this stage will not make any\par difference, unless it is to levels high enough to make the\par market re-evaluate its risk/reward parameters," said Fong\par Cheng Hong, an economist at Nomura Singapore.\par    Following two previous raises that saw the one month rate\par hiked to 45% from 22%, and then subsequently to 50%, the\par latest increase was widely regarded as insufficient to\par support the rupiah while considerations of Indonesian\par political risk still dominate the market.\par    Late in Asian trading the U.S. dollar was quoted at\par IDR9,650, up from IDR8,675 towards the close of trading on\par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  05-07-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0719EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du57015jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
