\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down; Bank Negara Believed Active \b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 1998\par 11:23\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The market's negative sentiment\par toward the Japanese yen again dragged Southeast Asia's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower during Asian trading hours on Monday.\par    Although \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders cited issues as diverse\par as the escalating violence of student protests in Indonesia\par and Malaysia's water shortage as grounds to sell regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yen's weakness remained the dominant theme as\par the Malaysian ringgit, the Singapore dollar, the Thai baht\par and the Indonesian rupiah all dropped along with the Japanese\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The Philippine peso dropped, too, although traders\par attributed the fall more to domestic nerves ahead of the\par national elections next month than to the depreciation of the\par yen.\par    "The dollar is looking bid across the board," said a\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at a U.K. bank in Singapore. He\par added, however, that the ringgit would have fallen further\par had it not been widely rumored that Bank Negara, the\par Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was selling U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollars to support\par the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Other traders echoed this opinion.\par    "We have seen heavy (U.S. dollar) selling from Kuala\par Lumpur," said an interbank trader at a U.S. bank in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "It looks as if Bank Negara may be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par    Late in Asian trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at\par 3.7830 ringgit (MYR), up from MYR3.7675 late on Friday, with\par offers around MYR3.7850 capping any further U.S. dollar\par appreciation in the short term, according to traders.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  04-27-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0523EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du4r011h8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
