\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Dn Late But Supported By BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fear \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 1998\par 12:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar finished Asian trading on Friday a touch lower against the U.S. dollar compared with its level late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Trading was extremely subdued, however, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  not straying out of a tight 44-point range throughout the day. \par \par \uc2  The session's activity was dominated by expectations that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the yen in support of the announcement late Friday of the contents of the Y16 trillion fiscal stimulus package put together by Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party. \par \par \uc2  'The talk is that G-7 central banks will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  later to support the yen, so no one is taking a chance on being caught long dollars,' said a trader at a U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The hesitance of market participants to be caught holding U.S. dollars lent the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  support, said traders. But as the fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifts, the coming week is likely to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar weaken once more, they added. \par \par \uc2  'There will definitely be good interest to buy dollars,' predicted the U.S. bank trader. \par \par \uc2  In late Asian trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.5900, up from S$1.5859 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit, meanwhile, is quoted at S$0.4225, little changed from S$0.4228 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's domestic money market, the overnight rate on local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits is quoted at 4.50%-4.625%, compared with 4.00%-4.25% late Thursday. The three-month rate is at 4.875%-5.00%, compared with 4.75%-4.875% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-04-98 \par \par \uc2  1048GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4o03gnf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
