\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Flat Late-AM; Mkt Wary Of Pushing S$ Higher \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 06:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is flat to a touch higher against the U.S. dollar in late morning trading Monday compared with its level in Asia late Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 0345 GMT (10:45 P.M. Sunday EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.5890, down a fraction from S$1.5900 toward the close of the previous session Friday. \par \par \uc2  Following the Singapore dollar's strengthening over recent weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are nervous of pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher lest they provoke \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The MAS, the island republic's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was widely rumored to have been selling Singapore dollars for U.S. dollars last week, in an effort to check the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. \par \par \uc2  There is currently significant interest to buy U.S. dollars stationed around S$1.5800, which should provide support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short term, say traders. If the S$1.5800 level is broken, the U.S. dollar is likely to fall rapidly to S$1.5500 before finding its floor, they add. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the ringgit is at S$0.4439, down a touch from S$0.4459 late Friday. In the medium term, the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen capped at S$0.4500, say traders. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's domestic money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 2.75%-3.00%, compared with 2.875%-3.00% late Friday. The three-month rate is at 4.5625%-4.6875%, down from 4.75%-4.875% on Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0405GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3u02oxj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
