\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Strong Singapore dollar soothes Asia  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 834 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 10:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 27 (Reuters) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lurched higher in late Friday trade as the Singapore dollar suddenly burst out of a drowsy range on rumoured buying by the Brunei Investment Agency. \par \par \uc2  Talk that Brunei, whose \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged to the Singapore dollar, had bought a large amount of Sing dollars, pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the 1.59 barrier against its U.S. counterpart, to a high of 1.5850. \par \par \uc2  "I think the market was just caught by surprise and a lot of stops were triggered. Everything seemed so quiet in the morning," a U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  near the U.S. dollar's highs thwarted a further rise in the Singapore dollar, but dealers said it would now target the 1.56 level. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to smooth sharp moves in the exchange rate. It does not typically comment on these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's rise also lifted the Malaysian ringgit out of its lethargy, taking it to a high of 3.57. \par \par \uc2  But traders said the ringgit's rise was being blocked by dollar bids below 3.55 per dollar, making the 3.50 level an increasingly difficult target amid anxiety about Thursday's riots at an immigration deportation centre in Malaysia, in which nine people were reported killed. \par \par \uc2  "If we fail to see 3.50 broken next week, the ringgit could be in for a very messy stretch," a senior European bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Malaysian Trade Minister Rafidah Aziz said the ringgit was expected to strengthen but probably not return to its previous level around 2.50 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  She said she did not want to see interest rates rise because this would raise costs for industry. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, Indonesia's debt problems remained in the spotlight as the market awaited details of how Jakarta planned to deal with $74 billion worth of corporate debt and when the IMF might release its next instalment of cash to the country. \par \par \uc2  The head of the IMF team in Jakarta, Hubert Neiss, said Indonesia's formula to resolve the debt crisis relied heavily on a model used by Mexico in the early 1980s. \par \par \uc2  Under that programme, the Mexican government assumed the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses of companies' loans but not the loans themselves. \par \par \uc2  Neiss told reporters after a meeting with Indonesian officials that he needed time to respond to the proposal and various other plans were also being discussed. \par \par \uc2  Key Japanese Finance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara said there was no consensus on Indonesia's corporate debt at the Manila framework meeting of finance and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputies from the Asia-Pacific region. \par \par \uc2  He said international banks had yet to agree on a delay in the repayment of Indonesian corporate debt. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia managing director Miranda Gultom said in Tokyo Indonesia was still reviewing proposals to stabilise the rupiah, including a trading band and a managed floating exchange rate, after shelving plans for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah dipped slightly in late trade, but remained underpinned by Bank Indonesia's sharp rate hikes early in the week. \par \par \uc2  Singapore Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong said the city-state would launch a bilateral trade financing scheme with Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  He said the trade guarantee should be backed by at least US$2 billion, which would come from Singapore's pledge to the IMF rescue package for Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  The plan follows what Goh described as a lack of interest from Group of Seven nations in his original proposal for a multi-lateral trade financing scheme. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso rebounded sharply from a weak open due to dollar inflows to the local stock market and a lack of corporate dollar demand. Traders said it could soon target the 36 level to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it expected the current account deficit to fall to 3.2 percent of gross national product this year, from 4.9 percent in 1997. It said the current account deficit stood at $4.303 billion by the end of 1997. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht remained sandwiched between dollar demand from domestic firms and offshore sales, keeping it in a tight band, though dealers said the market continued to target the 35 level. \par \par \uc2  The IMF's Thailand representative, Reza Moghadam, said the baht's recent appreciation would help in servicing its debt and reduce inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  He also praised the government's progress in implementing economic reforms and said Thailand could have more funds if necessary. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won strengthened as traders unwound dollar positions after the World Bank approved a $2 billion loan to the country. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar dipped fractionally while forwards softened after the Hong Kong Association of Banks said deposit rates would be cut by 25 basis points to 5.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered Bank and Hang Seng Bank said they would cut their prime rates by 25 basis points from Monday. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3r08joh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
