\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Higher Early, But Seen Toppish \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 02:36\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are\par stronger against the U.S. dollar early in Asian trading\par Thursday after an overnight run-up. Many market participants,\par however, question how much further regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can\par rise in the short term, suspecting the current rally may be\par nearing its top.\par    In overnight trading the Singapore dollar hit S$1.5950\par against the U.S. dollar, its highest level since Dec. 1. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has since slipped back, however, and traders are\par reluctant to push it higher, afraid that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the island republic's de facto\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent further\par strengthening.\par    "The authorities are sniffing around. They have already\par been in this morning," said a trader at a Singapore bank,\par saying that the MAS had bought U.S. dollars near the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's low.\par    At 0125 GMT (8:25 p.m. Wednesday EST) the U.S. dollar is\par quoted at S$1.5987, down from S$1.6044 late in Asia on\par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    In the short term, say traders, S$1.5950 will remain\par firmly supported by corporate bids, as well as the threat of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The ringgit has also pushed higher in early trading,\par although that too is looking toppish at current levels, say\par traders.\par    "The ringgit is not going anywhere fast right now," said\par a trader at a regional bank, adding that the market view of\par Bank Negara's annual report, which was released late\par Wednesday, is neutral to slightly negative.\par    The U.S. dollar is currently quoted at 3.5900 ringgit\par (MYR), down from MYR3.6420 in late trading the day before.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  03-25-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2036EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du3q00rxn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
