\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Ends Up, But Well Down From Early High \b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 11:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar ended Asian trading hours on Thursday a touch higher than its level late on Wednesday, but down sharply from a four-month high reached in early trading. \par \par \uc2  An overnight run-up in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saw the U.S. dollar fall to S$1.5950, its lowest level since Dec. 1. \par \par \uc2  As Asian trading got under way, however, the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated abruptly on heavy sales from domestic banks, leading some traders to suspect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The city state's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said, was buying up U.S. dollars at S$1.5950 in order to curb what it regards as excessive local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia the U.S. dollar had recovered from its earlier low to trade at S$1.5977, down from S$1.6044 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's domestic money market the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 2.50%-2.75%, up from 2.25%-2.50% late Wednesday. The three-month rate was at 4.75%-5.00%, compared with 4.75%-4.875% late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-03-98 \par \par \uc2  1028GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3q02lid\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgo