\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Early But Off 4-Mo High; MAS Sales Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 03:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is higher against the U.S. dollar in early trading Thursday, having hit a four-month high in overnight trading. \par \par \uc2  But the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's potential for further strengthening is limited by the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say traders. \par \par \uc2  'The authorities are sniffing around. They have already been in this morning,' said a trader at a Singapore bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, the island republic's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had bought U.S. dollars near the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's low to curtail the Singapore dollar's rally, he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0200 GMT (9 p.m. Wednesday EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.5993, above its overnight low of S$1.5950, but down from S$1.6044 late in Asia on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In the short term, say traders, S$1.5950 will remain firmly supported by corporate bids, as well as the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although market participants are reluctant to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar higher against the U.S. dollar, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seeing buying interest against the ringgit, say traders. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is currently trading at S$0.4475, up from S$0.4416 late on Wednesday, but down from an overnight high of S$0.4491. A level of S$0.4500 is seen as the ringgit's short-term top, say traders. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's domestic money market the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 2.75%-3.00%, up from 2.25%-2.50% late Wednesday. The three-month rate is flat at 4.75%-4.875%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0214GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3q02kp6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
