\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Dn Late On Corporate Sales, Ringgit Drop \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 10:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is down against the U.S. dollar in late Asian trading on Tuesday, after dipping sharply in early trading. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on what traders said was heavy buying of U.S. dollars by a Singapore bank on behalf of a local corporate. \par \par \uc2  The drop spurred other market participants to take their profits from the previous day's run-up, according to traders, who also cited a fall in the ringgit and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the rally become over-extended, as reasons for the sell-off. \par \par \uc2  At 0930 GMT (4:30 a.m. EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6065, up from S$1.5995 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Following market disappointment at a key policy-setting speech made Tuesday afternoon by Malaysian finance minister Anwar Ibrahim, there is little chance of further Singapore dollar strengthening in the short-term, said traders, with support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen at S$1.60. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the ringgit is quoted at S$0.4414, down from S$0.4509. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's domestic money market the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 3.25%-3.50%, up from 2.75%-3.00% late on Monday. The three-month rate is at 4.75%-5.00%, flat compared with the rate late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0956GMT \par \par \uc2