\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Lower Early; Mkt Nervous Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 03:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)-- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is down in early trading Tuesday, after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed convincingly to break through resistance at S$1.60 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Although the U.S. dollar traded to an early low of S$1.5985, buying from local corporations pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher again, spurring market players to cover their U.S.-dollar short positions. \par \par \uc2  'I don't see the Singapore dollar going anywhere. S$1.5950 to S$1.5980 should provide good support (for the U.S. dollar) for the time being,' said a trader at a U.K. bank in the island republic. \par \par \uc2  At 0205 GMT (9:05 p.m. Monday EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6095, up from S$1.5995 in late Asian trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  Should a package of economic initiatives to be unveiled later Tuesday by Malaysian Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim meet market expectations, the Singapore dollar may trail the ringgit higher, say traders. \par \par \uc2  The run-up is likely to be modest, however, given the market's fear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb what it regards as any excessive strength in the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's domestic money market the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 2.50%-2.75%, down from 2.75%-3.00% late Monday. The three-month rate is at 4.625%-4.875%, a touch lower than 4.75%-5.00%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0217GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3o02gsk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
