\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Higher Late, Shadowing Ringgit's Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 229 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 11:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is higher against the U.S. dollar in late trading in Asia on Monday, buoyed by the appreciation of the Malaysian ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Investors bought the ringgit on Monday, said traders, in anticipation that economic initiatives to be announced on Tuesday by Malaysian Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim, will prove positive for the country's battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In response, the Singapore dollar also gained against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite some purchases of the ringgit against the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's rise was damped by sales of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Singapore banks, which led traders to speculate that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the island republic's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to cap excessive appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia the U.S. dollar had broken through key support at S$1.60 to reach S$1.5989, down from S$1.6074 late in Asia on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's domestic money market the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 2.75%-3.00%, up from 2.00%-2.25% late on Friday. The three-month rate is at 4.75%-5.00%, up a touch from 4.50%-4.75%. \par \par \uc2  - By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-03-98 \par \par \uc2  1006GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3n0